# Courier-PCP / SqWebMail PAM Configuration
# This file configures the Pluggable Authentication Modules (PAM) stack for the SqWebMail daemon.
# It delegates authentication and account management to the common PAM stacks.
# No dynamic variables are used; this is a static configuration file managed by the package.
#
# The following includes pull in the system-wide default PAM policies.
# To customize authentication (e.g., LDAP, RADIUS, or specific password policies),
# edit the files included here or replace the @include directives with explicit
# auth/account/password/session stack definitions.

# Standard authentication mechanisms (e.g., shadow passwords, LDAP, etc.)
@include common-auth

# Account management (e.g., account lockout, expiration, allowed hosts)
@include common-account

# Password management (e.g., password strength, expiration, change policies)
@include common-password